# {{SITE_NAME}}

{{PURPOSE}}

A DjangoCMS 5 site (Bootstrap 5.3, light/dark mode, mobile friendly) scaffolded by the
`djangocms-agent` skill. It ships a landing page, an About page and a "Style & Capabilities" page that
renders every verified plugin.

## Quick start

    python3 -m venv venv
    venv/bin/pip install -r requirements-dev.txt  # requirements.txt = production only
    export DJANGO_DEBUG=1 DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=dev
    venv/bin/python manage.py migrate
    venv/bin/python manage.py createsuperuser
    venv/bin/python manage.py seed_pages
    venv/bin/python manage.py seed_site
    venv/bin/python manage.py runserver 8010

The seed commands also set the django Site (shown in the admin and the CMS toolbar, otherwise the stock
`example.com`) to the site name and to the domain in `SITE_DOMAIN` (default `localhost`; re-run `seed_site` after
changing it).

Open http://localhost:8010/ (use the first free port at or above 8000; check with `ss -ltn`) and sign in at http://localhost:8010/admin/. Edit pages by adding
`?edit` to a URL while logged in. `DJANGO_DEBUG=1` is development only; production needs
`DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` and `DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (see `.env.example`).

## Verify

    bin/verify.sh

Runs `check`, `makemigrations --check`, the tests, seed idempotency, and Playwright screenshots
(desktop and mobile) of the main pages into `verify-shots/`. Look at them. Requires
Playwright for the visual step; install it once in a scratch venv, not system Python:

    python3 -m venv /tmp/pw-venv && /tmp/pw-venv/bin/pip install playwright && /tmp/pw-venv/bin/playwright install chromium
    PLAYWRIGHT_PYTHON=/tmp/pw-venv/bin/python bin/verify.sh

Without it `bin/verify.sh` ends `VERIFY RESULT: INCOMPLETE`. The verification server runs with
`DJANGO_DEBUG_TOOLBAR=0`.

## Login throttling and the theme toggle

- **Login throttling (django-axes):** 5 failed admin/CMS logins (`DJANGO_LOGIN_FAILURE_LIMIT`) lock that username + IP
  for 60 minutes (`DJANGO_LOGIN_COOLOFF_MINUTES`; 0 = until an operator unlocks). While locked the right password is
  refused too and the visitor sees a 429 page; other pages and users are unaffected. Unlock: `python manage.py axes_reset`
  (everyone), `axes_reset_ip IP`, `axes_reset_username NAME` or `axes_reset_ip_username IP NAME`, run where the app
  runs. `axes_list_attempts` shows what is recorded, `/admin/axes/` has the logs.
  `DJANGO_LOGIN_FAILURE_LIMIT=0` turns it off; `DJANGO_LOGIN_LOCKOUT_BY=ip` counts per address only (stricter, but one
  attacker locks everyone behind that address). Counters live in the database, so all gunicorn workers share them.
  The client IP is `REMOTE_ADDR`; `X-Forwarded-For` is **only** trusted with `DJANGO_BEHIND_PROXY=1` (then the entry
  `DJANGO_PROXY_COUNT` hops from the right, default 1: your proxy must append to or overwrite that header and be the
  only way to reach the app port). Without a proxy flag a forged header cannot dodge or cause a lockout. Behind a proxy
  that does NOT send the header, every client shares the proxy's address.
- **Theme toggle:** the header button switches light/dark and remembers the choice in the browser (`localStorage` key
  `theme`); without a stored choice the page follows the OS, live. Without JavaScript the OS media query still applies
  and the button is hidden.

{{DOCKER_README}}## Known warnings and development extras

- `treebeard.E001` (a warning about `cms.PageManager`) is printed on every `manage.py` command. It comes
  from django-cms 5.1.3 with django-treebeard 5.3.x, is upstream, and is harmless until treebeard 6; do not
  try to fix it in this project.
- With `DJANGO_DEBUG=1` a small green tab on the right edge of pages is the django-debug-toolbar handle (not
  the CMS toolbar). It only exists when DEBUG is on; set `DJANGO_DEBUG_TOOLBAR=0` to remove it.

